{
  "_comment": [
    "Coordinates for every city named in fuel-prices-for-be-assessment.csv that html/cities.js does",
    "not cover. Without this, those truck stops could not be placed on a map and would be dropped",
    "from the planner. Every priced truck stop in the file is loaded, including the 112 in Canadian",
    "provinces, so most entries here are Canadian cities the US city table was never going to have.",
    "",
    "'aliases' map a price-file city onto a city already in the table that is the same place under",
    "another spelling. 'coordinates' are places the table does not have at all. All of them came",
    "from Nominatim (OpenStreetMap), and each was accepted only when the ISO 3166-2 subdivision it",
    "returned matched the state or province the price file asked for, so a same-named place",
    "elsewhere is never used.",
    "",
    "Keys are '<normalized city>|<lowercase state>', normalized by",
    "planner.services.geocoding.normalize, which is why Fort Erie appears as 'ft erie' and",
    "Saint-Liboire as 'st liboire'.",
    "",
    "Check coverage with : python manage.py check_prices",
    "Regenerate with     : python manage.py check_prices --geocode-missing"
  ],
  "aliases": {
    "brookpark|oh": "brook park",
    "elizabethport|nj": "elizabeth"
  },
